@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="d-flex justify-content-center py-3">
    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 w-100 create-card">
        <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
            <h1 class="h2 fw-bold mb-3">Privacy</h1>
            <p class="text-muted">This page explains what VotingApp stores about you and why.</p>

            <h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">What we store</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Your account:</strong> full name, email, username, date of birth, and your password in
                    hashed form. We cannot read your password.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your activity:</strong> the polls you create and the votes you cast. A vote is linked to
                        your account so that each person can vote only once in a poll. The app never shows other users which
                        option you chose.</li>
                        <li><strong>Photos</strong> you upload for polls and for choices.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Cookies</h2>
                    <p>The app uses one cookie to keep you signed in, and one security cookie that protects its forms. There are
                        no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

                        <h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Other websites</h2>
                        <p>Some fonts and scripts are loaded from Google Fonts and from the DataTables CDN, so those services can
                            see your IP address when a page loads.</p>

                            <h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Your choices</h2>
                            <p class="mb-0">You can delete the polls you created at any time. To remove your account, contact the
                                administrator.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>